  "capabilities": [
    "Stage01 project conditions remain explicit user business declarations; none is never auto-confirmed.",
    "Stage01 payload 0.9.0 is validated before an in-memory 0.9.1 migration candidate is created.",
    "Stage01 migration preserves existing business values, unknown extension keys, and explicitly empty organization arrays.",
    "Revit-native fields use per-field authority and drift evidence instead of one global overwrite priority.",
    "NoRecord forms use current Revit ProjectInformation and ProjectPosition values while retaining target units m, m² and °.",
    "Current Stage01 payloads are compared with live Revit evidence without silent overwrite.",
    "Stage02 and Stage03 consume only Current Stage01 storage, never an unconfirmed migration candidate.",
    "Stage03 defaults to strict mode and supports explicitly reasoned forced-test mode without bypassing technical corruption.",
    "Autodesk IFC4 RAW is protected from in-place mutation and final H-IFC publication requires exact disk reread validation.",
    "IFCFlux external status remains IFCFLUX_MANUAL_PENDING until user inspection.",
    "Manual Revit UI and MCP use the same Stage01, Stage02 and Stage03 services.",
    "The MCP surface contains 13 approved business tools and exposes no arbitrary Revit API execution.",
    "Runtime version, build number, commit SHA and DLL path come from the Revit process loaded assembly.",
    "Installer evidence records normalized product version, build number, commit SHA and binary hashes.",
    "Stage03 defaults export output to the active Revit model directory and remembers manual directory overrides per canonical RVT path.",
    "Stage03 forced test mode no longer requires a reason string in either the native workspace or MCP tool contract.",
    "Stage03 can open or create the currently configured export root folder before or after export."
